# Workers Assets serves everything with `max-age=0, must-revalidate` by default, so a warm reload spends fifty-odd
# conditional requests before the login screen can do anything. The sprite and sound sets are named files that change
# only when a new one is drawn, so they can be cached outright; renaming one is how you bust it.
#
# assets/osrs is deliberately NOT here. player.json and models.bin.gz are a matched pair — the json holds the byte
# offsets into the bin — and a cache that can hold one without the other is a cache that can hand a player garbage.
# The code files stay on must-revalidate too: a stale game.js against a fresh worker is the bug this project's socket
# hello exists to catch.
/assets/i07/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/assets/c07/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/assets/sound/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
# a page opened straight from disk (file://) reads the map tables and sounds from the live site
/assets/map07/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
